window.docContents[103].resolve({"/Browse-the-paper-and-supplement/#sample-8":{"contents":"Supplement lemma S4.10 · selected declaration. Selected Lean declaration\n\nRecorded formal verification pass. \n\nDeclaration: HRS.Whole.far_derivatives_proof.\n\nSource: HRS/MS/SuppU2.lean, line 17.\n\nExact source excerpt. It may include adjacent declarations or end before the proof does; open the source file for full context.\n\ntheorem far_derivatives_proof : type_of% @HRS.Whole.far_derivatives := by\n  intro d hd s hs0 hsd k L hL\n  exact ⟨u2_partA hd s hs0 hsd k L hL, fun M Λρ => u2_partB hd s hs0 hsd k L hL M Λρ⟩\n\nend HRS.Whole\n\n\nRecorded verification: theorem check passed.\n\n","context":"Fluctuations of Riesz gases\u0009Browse the paper and supplement\u0009S4. Thermal fields and support-independent correctors","header":"3.15.1. Far-field derivatives of the nonlocal term","id":"/Browse-the-paper-and-supplement/#sample-8"},"/Relaxation-on-moving-windows/#s11-cubic-tensor":{"contents":"For preparation  and shift , the cubic path tensor is specified by the three-observation formula of Theorem S2.1(iii) at the constant trajectory . It is a symmetric element of . Choose three times , smooth oscillator tests , and put . For each such choice there must exist cross-covariance densities  for all . They satisfy  and, for every oscillator test ,\n\nwith integrable product. For every such family of densities, the tensor evaluated on the trilinear form  must equal the three terms of that formula at the physical times . All its spatial and time integrals must exist as specified there.\n\n","context":"Fluctuations of Riesz gases\u0009Relaxation on moving windows","header":"6.7. The cubic path tensor","id":"/Relaxation-on-moving-windows/#s11-cubic-tensor"}});